/*
3828. Final Element After Subarray Deletions
Leetcode Link : https://leetcode.com/problems/final-element-after-subarray-deletions/
Approach
Initially:
 
Array length = m
Alice is allowed to remove m − 1 elements
 
That means Alice can:
 
Leave exactly one element
End the game immediately
Because removal must be contiguous, Alice has only two possible ways to remove m − 1 elements:
Case 1: Keep the first element
Case 2: Keep the last element
 
On move 1, Alice can force the game to end with either:
 
nums[0] or nums[m−1]
 
No matter what Bob wants.
So Alice’s guaranteed outcome set is:
 
max { nums[0], nums[m-1] }
 
Why delaying NEVER helps Alice
 
Let's say
 
If Alice does not end the game on move 1:
The array still has ≥ 2 elements
 
Bob gets a turn
Bob’s only goal is to destroy Alice’s best possible future
 
Bob will always:
 
Remove subarrays that eliminate large candidates
Preserve smaller ones
From this point on:
 
Alice can no longer guarantee any value better than what she could force earlier
 
Any "better" outcome depends on Bob cooperating which he won’t ( better as in better than what Alice was getting initally )
 
If the array size is 1, game has ended before it even started so we can exit there itself
 
Complexity
Time complexity:
O(1)
 
Space complexity:
O(N)
*/
/**
* @param {number[]} nums
* @return {number}
*/
var finalElement = function(nums) {
    let n = nums.length;
        
        if (n == 1) {
            return nums[0];
        }
        
        return Math.max(nums[0], nums[n - 1]);
};
